1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:06,140
I still think we should call first before we go all the way to Boston to see your

2
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:08,460
folks. Jason, they just tell us not to come.

3
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:10,740
Oh, here, here, let me...

4
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,400
I'll get those for you,

5
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:15,620
Dad. Carol, honey, we're almost ready.

6
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,140
Were you speaking to me?

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,880
No one spoke to me when this trip was being planned.

8
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:25,540
Honey, we didn't know we were going until last night.

9
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:28,200
Carol, we're worried about Grandma and Grandpa.

10
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,680
Oh, Maggie, I think you're overreacting.

11
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:33,840
Then why did they call and cancel the trip at the last minute?

12
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:36,360
And why did my dad say everything was swell?

13
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:38,760
Uh, because it is.

14
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:43,780
No, Jason, my father doesn't use words like swell, good, or nice.

15
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:45,900
Hmm. Certainly not when I'm in the room.

16
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:48,780
Let's go! Let's go!

17
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:51,860
Let's go! Well, you sure are excited about this, Ben.

18
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:52,940
Are you kidding?

19
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:58,180
Grandpa's gonna let me use his nightstick and his handcuffs and even wear his badge!

20
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:01,320
Hey, maybe you'll get fingerprinted, too.

21
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:08,260
Wow! Well, Dad, again, I just want to thank you for letting me stay home and earn

22
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:09,640
some extra money helping Mr.

23
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:10,840
Sacks fertilize his lawn.

24
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:15,520
I'm sure that earning money will teach me a new respect for the dollar and help me

25
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:16,560
grow as a person.

26
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:20,160
Bet you'd be pretty good at spreading manure, too.

27
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:25,420
I am so sorry that I'm gonna miss that sing -along around Grandma's piano.

28
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:33,300
Yeah. Well, just remember, if you have any problems, here, you call the Kuzmans next

29
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:36,160
door, and only one guest stays over tonight.

30
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:38,500
This is not fair!

31
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:42,740
No one thought that old Carol might have other plans.

32
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:49,040
No one in this entire house treated me like a real, living, breathing human person.

33
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:50,880
Carol, get in the car.

34
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:56,880
Bye, sweetheart. Oh, and, Mike, I know everything will be fine, because if it

35
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,820
isn't... You'll be grounded until you're 35.

36
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,760
Enough said. Bye, Mom.

37
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:04,740
Bye, Dad. See you tomorrow, Mike.

38
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:05,780
All right, have fun.

39
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:06,760
Bye -bye. Bye.

40
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:15,760
Yeah! Show me that smile again

41
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:25,780
Don't waste another minute on your crying We're nowhere near the end The best is

42
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:34,080
ready to begin Oh, oh, oh, oh As long as we guide each other

43
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:43,080
We got the world spinning right in our hands Baby, you and me, we gotta be The

44
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:51,840
luckiest dreamers who never quit dreaming As long as we keep on giving We can take

45
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:54,420
anything that comes our way.

46
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:58,760
Baby rain or shine all the time.

47
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:02,420
We got each other sharing the laughter.

48
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:15,500
Ben, wait for us.

49
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,780
I gotta go to the bathroom.

50
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:21,540
We want to surprise Grandma and Grandpa together.

51
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:26,080
If Grandpa starts frisking me before I go, I'll surprise him all right.

52
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,120
Hi. Like, hi.

53
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:34,240
I'm, uh, Ed and Kate's daughter, Maggie.

54
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:38,180
Good. Excuse us, please.

55
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:41,040
Oh, should you just walk in there like that?

56
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:45,580
Well, we should not stand out here in a cold waiting for some jerk to open the door.

57
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:49,460
Ooh, uh... Who are they?

58
00:03:57,980 --> 00:04:01,540
Mom, are these people the relatives you don't send Christmas cards to?

59
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:05,080
I'm gonna try and find Grandma and Grandpa.

60
00:04:05,660 --> 00:04:06,820
Ah! Ha -ha!

61
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:07,860
How are ya, folks?

62
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:08,740
Come on in.

63
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:11,040
Ha -ha. Oh, I see you brought your luggage.

64
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:12,240
Well, don't worry.

65
00:04:12,340 --> 00:04:14,040
We'll try to close this deal by nightfall.

66
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:16,060
Ha -ha. The kiddies, too.

67
00:04:16,060 --> 00:04:16,920
This is so nice.

68
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:19,980
Cocktail Frank? My name's not Frank.

69
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:23,740
Who are you?

70
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:24,500
Who am I?

71
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:25,700
I don't know you.

72
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:26,560
I don't know him.

73
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,820
Harry Biddle. Great American Dream Realty Company.

74
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:31,900
This house is for sale?

75
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:34,860
Oh, yes. Where are the owners?

76
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:37,640
Oh, well, the sellers are never present for the showing.

77
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:40,380
Especially sellers who have put 30 years into a place.

78
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:41,440
This would break their heart.

79
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:47,540
I'm sure. Well, honey, they haven't sold it yet.

80
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:49,080
You folks are interested in this house?

81
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:54,040
Deeply. Oh, well, then let me point out some of the fine features of this timeless

82
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:57,580
classic. If you do, I'm going to cry.

83
00:04:58,260 --> 00:05:01,440
Pardon? Why are they selling?

84
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:04,240
You're not interested in hearing about the house?

85
00:05:04,660 --> 00:05:05,920
I love this house.

86
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:11,000
I do my homework right by the fireplace, waiting for my daddy to come home and hang

87
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,980
up his gun and give me a hug.

88
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:15,540
Why are they selling?

89
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:19,720
Oh, well, uh, I can't really violate their confidence.

90
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:25,300
But I will say, retirement income, a loan payment, disaster, phew!

91
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:29,660
Oh! It's all right.

92
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:30,520
I'm her psychiatrist.

93
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:32,100
Oh, well, uh, can I do anything?

94
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:35,260
Yes, you could just, uh, give us a moment alone, please.

95
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:38,380
Thank you. Come on, Maggie, sweetheart.

96
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:39,760
Come on, we'll look into this.

97
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:42,220
Selling this house has to be breaking their hearts.

98
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:44,000
I know. Why didn't they come to us for help?

99
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,840
Oh, my father's pride.

100
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:50,000
There's no way he could ask us for money knowing the way he feels about what you do

101
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:50,760
for a living.

102
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:55,180
What? Forget I said that.

103
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:57,640
I mean, I knew he didn't care for me.

104
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:59,700
I didn't think he hated my entire profession.

105
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:02,480
Oh, well, honey, it's not that he hates your profession.

106
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:04,240
It's just that he doesn't know what it is.

107
00:06:05,180 --> 00:06:09,060
Oh. So now, after 17 years, I find this out?

108
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:13,400
Now, what good would it have done to let you know that he thinks you're a quack.

109
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:19,200
A quack? Jason, can we talk about this later?

110
00:06:19,820 --> 00:06:23,380
Now, I don't want this house sold until we get a chance to talk to Mom and Dad.

111
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:29,180
Sure, sure. Genuine, laughed and plaster, unreal, two by four studs.

112
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:32,100
Excuse me, I don't mean to interrupt, Harry.

113
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:35,280
No problem. What you were saying over there confused me.

114
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:39,060
Were the victims' bodies found in this room or all through the house?

115
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:44,040
Hey, he's so tall!

116
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:44,640
He's so tall!

117
00:06:45,420 --> 00:06:45,740
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

118
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:48,060
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

119
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:49,100
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

120
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:52,120
This is life as it should be.

121
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:58,960
Mike! Mike! Shhh, shh, shh, shh.

122
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,560
Ah! Man, that was good.

123
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:03,700
Guys, how you doing?

124
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:04,180
Hey, you're early.

125
00:07:04,220 --> 00:07:05,240
I didn't even order the pizza yet.

126
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:05,960
Let me do it.

127
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:07,560
Uh, my cousin Gus works for Paradise Pizza.

128
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:08,360
I can get us a discount.

129
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:10,540
All right. So, Mikey, what's the accent?

130
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:11,800
Not much, not much.

131
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:14,100
We're gonna eat a little pizza, watch a little TV.

132
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:17,800
TV? Mike, your folks ain't home.

133
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:21,100
This is like the chance of a lifetime and you wanna watch TV?

134
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:24,360
It's already started.

135
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:26,840
Mike, what could be so important that...

136
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:29,500
Wow. So, like, when'd you get cable?

137
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:32,680
This is great.

138
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:35,040
Gus doesn't let us have the pizzas for nothing.

139
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:38,120
All right! If he and a couple friends can stop by after work.

140
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,500
How many? I don't think we should have more.

141
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,940
You mentioned women.

142
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:50,100
Alright. ["Best of Best Got to Best"]

143
00:07:58,140 --> 00:08:01,440
Is the rest of the trip gonna be this much fun?

144
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:06,120
Carol, why don't you and Ben go watch TV in Grandpa's den?

145
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:08,780
Great! Sure, it's great for you.

146
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:10,380
You get to spend time with me.

147
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:14,060
Ben, don't you go touching any of your grandpa's police stuff.

148
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:15,420
You know me.

149
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:19,120
Jason, we've got to help him.

150
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:22,000
I'm not so sure your dad wants our help.

151
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:23,340
Then again, what do I know?

152
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,680
I'm just a licensed quack.

153
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:26,780
Oh, Jason. Bring Slime back!

154
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:31,020
Daddy! Ed, you almost shot Jason.

155
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:35,940
Well, they're not supposed to be here.

156
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:38,820
Uh, no one's supposed to be here.

157
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:41,420
Oh, Mom, how are you?

158
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:42,840
It's so good to see you.

159
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:45,220
I'm fine. Aw.

160
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:48,600
Did you say you were coming and I forgot?

161
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:50,920
No, Mom. No.

162
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,760
Always a pleasure to see you.

163
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:55,000
Daddy, Daddy, Daddy!

164
00:08:55,760 --> 00:09:00,460
Duncan! So, what's this about selling the house?

165
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:05,220
Uh, well, we thought we'd do this retirement thing right.

166
00:09:05,220 --> 00:09:08,100
Move into a smaller place with less upkeep.

167
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:11,200
A condo. Grandma!

168
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,500
Grandpa! Carol, honey!

169
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:16,340
Ooh! Look how she's grown.

170
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:19,160
Ha! Where's Mikey?

171
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:21,840
Oh, well, Mike couldn't come.

172
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,140
Grandpa! Is that Benny?

173
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:26,700
Yes. Look out.

174
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:31,360
All right, come out with your hands up.

175
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:35,580
I can't. Carol handcuffed me to the chair!

176
00:09:37,740 --> 00:09:40,240
Ah -ha! Watch the door.

177
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:41,920
I'm gonna rough him up.

178
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:44,320
Ha -ha! Get your back to me.

179
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:46,440
Let's go. I'm getting so excited.

180
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:47,540
I'm getting too.

181
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:49,860
Ah. Well, we're gonna fix a little dinner.

182
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:50,560
Come on, Ben.

183
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:52,180
Let your dad and granddad talk.

184
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:54,580
Uh, I don't think that'll be necessary.

185
00:09:54,580 --> 00:09:56,220
No, he could lay here if you...

186
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,100
Come on, Ben.

187
00:09:57,100 --> 00:09:58,920
You can peel potatoes with the other prisoners.

188
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:14,320
Wow! Daddy, if you and Mom are having financial problems, we would be...

189
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:15,840
No, no, no.

190
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:16,680
Things are swell.

191
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:19,540
They're fine. Even good.

192
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:24,580
Dad, any money you need, Jason and I would be more than happy to help.

193
00:10:25,020 --> 00:10:30,420
Maggie, just in case you can't remember, little girl, I kept a roof over your head

194
00:10:30,420 --> 00:10:33,140
and food on the table for over 18 years.

195
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:35,480
Till he came along anyway.

196
00:10:36,380 --> 00:10:41,320
Daddy. Damn it, I can still take care of your mom and myself without your charity.

197
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:43,780
Ed, Ed, Ed, please.

198
00:10:44,780 --> 00:10:48,500
There's no reason for you to turn down this offer just because of how you feel about

199
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:50,060
me. Jason, let's not mention.

200
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:50,360
No, no, no, no.

201
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:53,880
Your dad should overcome his feelings about me and save this house.

202
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:59,360
Why hurt your wife, your daughter, yourself, all in the name of some foolish pride?

203
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:05,160
Foolish? Don't use your shrink talk on me!

204
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:10,700
The day I accept one dime of your money will be the day they bury me!

205
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,940
I think that went well, don't you?

206
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:29,340
Yeah, Jim, I'm sorry.

207
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:31,640
Jerry, listen. Call Bruce Vinneker.

208
00:11:32,060 --> 00:11:34,820
Tell the party central's at 15 Robin Hood Lane.

209
00:11:35,540 --> 00:11:37,440
Yeah. Uh, excuse me.

210
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:38,340
Slug, is it?

211
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:41,380
I don't think we should invite any more people.

212
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:43,040
But what's it to you?

213
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:44,220
Didn't you hear?

214
00:11:44,260 --> 00:11:45,560
The bozo that lives here?

215
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:46,980
Parrots are out of town.

216
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:51,220
Bozo A. Hey, you're Mike!

217
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:54,820
Remember me? Linda McManus.

218
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:57,180
We had a karate class together.

219
00:11:57,180 --> 00:11:59,440
Yeah, yeah, of course I remember you.

220
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:01,020
You have got killer hands.

221
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:03,660
Uh, I mean, I didn't mean...

222
00:12:03,660 --> 00:12:04,680
I know what you mean.

223
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:05,780
Mike, come here.

224
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:09,200
Would you excuse me for just a second?

225
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,580
Okay, but just a second.

226
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:17,460
Eddie! Michael, there are two guys out back throwing up and a guy upstairs shaving.

227
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:20,560
I mean, this has gotta be the coolest party I've ever been to!

228
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:24,400
Shaving? Mike, I need a couple bucks.

229
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:25,580
Your mom's car ran out of gas.

230
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:27,720
Eddie, you can't take my mom's car.

231
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:29,500
I didn't. Frank did.

232
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:32,980
Who's Frank? I thought you knew him.

233
00:12:33,460 --> 00:12:37,600
No! All right, Gus's pizza mobile wouldn't start, right?

234
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:39,920
So he calls Frank and says we'd have to pick up our own pizzas.

235
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,060
And since they're free, could we make a couple deliveries?

236
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:43,720
In my mom's car?

237
00:12:43,940 --> 00:12:45,400
What was Frank supposed to do?

238
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:46,620
What was Frank supposed to do?

239
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:48,580
What was Frank supposed to do?

240
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:49,720
All right, all right.

241
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:50,920
Relax, baby, it's under control.

242
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:53,780
Now, just give me a little gas money.

243
00:12:53,780 --> 00:12:54,780
I'm in my...

244
00:13:09,220 --> 00:13:14,220
Mom, make Dad take the money.

245
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:15,520
It's your home, too.

246
00:13:15,700 --> 00:13:17,460
Well, your father's the boss.

247
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:21,620
And on our wedding day, I promise to love, honor and obey.

248
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:24,400
Oh, Mom, Mom, Mom.

249
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:27,280
Every modern woman knows Obey is just a figure of speech.

250
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:30,760
Maybe that's why every modern woman seems to get divorced.

251
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:34,200
Kate, the kids are glued to the piano.

252
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:35,520
They're waiting for one of your songs.

